Z||000000||Mikeyg||03-24-2000||05:16 PM||||Can anyone tell me how much different year fieros weigh and hp for each ? 4&6 cylinders ? Also is there a major difference in suspension between 88 and previous? Is there someone who has done a v8 swap personally?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||03-24-2000||06:06 PM||||87 & 88 GT weigh in at about 2800lbs w/o driver. 86s, formulas and 4 bangers are lighter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||03-24-2000||06:09 PM||||88 had only the redesigned suspension (best)with 84 on up having gradual improvements. All V6 pulled 135hp except for 86.5 - 88 which pulled 140.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-25-2000||09:48 AM||||The V-6 weighs 44 pounds more than a 4cyl.<BR>A 350 V-8 weighs 86 pounds more than a V-6.<BR>Horse power for 4cyl is 90hp/100hp<BR>Horse power for V-6 is 135/140hp<BR>Horse power for V-8 is 275 to ????? (how fast do you want to go)<BR>The 88 suspension had unequal length A-arms, vented brakes, and rear sway bars on GT's<BR>As for Fiero vehicle weights. The Pontiac spec sheet for the 1986 Fieros lists the 4cyl coupe at 2450, The SE at 2520, and the GT at 2650. I do not know if the weights are the same for every year nor with which trans they used. I think a manual is lighter than an auto.<BR>||||reg||1
